  "suggestion": "Replace the generic blue cube with a stylized, low-poly animal character (e.g., a chicken or frog) with distinct geometry to create an emotional anchor. Break the visual rhythm of the terrain by introducing varied textures (grass tufts, flowers) and distinct lane types (wooden planks for the river, asphalt for roads) to create meaningful differentiation. Transform the HUD into a diegetic element, such as a wooden signpost or a floating cloud, to match the game's world. Apply a vibrant, high-saturation color palette with strong directional lighting and soft shadows to create depth and a 'game-ready' feel. Finally, stylize the controls to look like physical buttons or integrated game elements rather than standard UI widgets."
